# NFS exports on lenora. See exports(5).
#
# Managed from homelab/proxmox - edit here, not on the host. scripts/deploy.sh
# pushes this file and runs `exportfs -ra`.
#
# The LAN moved to 192.168.8.0/24 in October 2026, when the GL.iNet router
# replaced the Orange Livebox. This export still named the old 192.168.1.0/24
# until 11 October 2026, so nothing on the current LAN could mount it.
#
# all_squash + anonuid/anongid=65534 maps every client to nobody:nogroup, so
# the export grants no uid-based access to anything on hddpool. That is why a
# /24 is an acceptable granularity here.
#
# Containers on lenora do NOT use this: an unprivileged LXC cannot mount NFS,
# so they get /hddpool/media through the mp0 bind mount instead. This export is
# for machines that are not containers on this host.
# One line per address family - exports(5) has no syntax for "this host by
# either", and a client mounting over IPv6 is matched only by the IPv6 entry.
# The ULA, not the ISP prefix: the ULA is ours and stable, while
# 2a01:cb1c:d:3500::/64 renumbers with the lease and would silently stop
# matching. See wireguard/README.md, "Home LANs and the ISP's IPv6".
/hddpool/media	192.168.8.0/24(rw,sync,all_squash,anonuid=65534,anongid=65534,no_subtree_check)
/hddpool/media	fd33:5692:1834:1000::/64(rw,sync,all_squash,anonuid=65534,anongid=65534,no_subtree_check)
